<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Long Island Sound</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Long Island Sound is a tidal estuary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-ocean">Atlantic Ocean</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/connecticut">Connecticut</a> and Long Island, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, about 180 km long. Its northern shore was settled by English <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puritans">Puritans</a> from the 1630s, who founded New Haven and other coastal towns. It has since been a busy waterway for shipping, fishing and recreation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/long-island-sound.jpg" alt="Long Island Sound" width="316" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Decumanus at English Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wpdms_ev26188_long_island_sound.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
